DESCRIPTION:Allied Scholars for Animal Protection (ASAP at IU) is hosting 
 a multi-day visual memorial in Dunn Meadow ahead of Thanksgiving to raise
  awareness about animal agriculture and food system ethics.\nThe display 
 features small\, temporary yard flags placed in the grass\, with each fla
 g representing 10\,000 turkeys killed annually for Thanksgiving. The disp
 lay will expand progressively each day to visualize the scale of impact l
 eading up to the holiday. Chapter members will maintain\, monitor\, and s
 teward the setup daily\, pairing the visual display with an optional info
 rmational table to engage with passing students and answer questions. All
  materials will be completely removed at the conclusion of the event\, le
 aving the green space in its original condition. \n\nHosted by: Allied Sc
 holars for Animal Protection at Indiana University\n\nAdditional Informat
 ion can be found at: https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12979881
DTEND:20261121T013000Z
DTSTAMP:20261114T061319Z
DTSTART:20261116T130000Z
LOCATION:Dunn Meadow 2 (East side)
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Thanksgiving Turkey Memorial
UID:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12979881
