DESCRIPTION:Join the LGBTQ+ Culture Center for World AIDS Day\, an evening
  of remembrance\, reflection\, and hope featuring keynote speaker Ace Rob
 inson\, M.P.H.\, M.H.L.\, Director of Sexual & Gender Minority (Queer) We
 llness at Duke University. \nA nationally recognized HIV policy advocate 
 and population health expert\, Ace Robinson has spent more than two decad
 es advancing health equity and supporting communities disproportionately 
 impacted by HIV. Throughout his career\, he has held leadership roles wit
 h organizations including the National Minority AIDS Council (NMAC)\, Gay
  Men’s Health Crisis (GMHC)\, the Desmond Tutu Health Foundation in South
  Africa\, and the David Geffen School of Medicine at UCLA. \nIn his keyno
 te\, “Willing Our Way to End the HIV Epidemic\,” Robinson will explore th
 e progress made in HIV prevention and treatment\, the challenges that rem
 ain\, and the collective action needed to build a future free from stigma
 \, discrimination\, and health inequities. \nFollowing the keynote\, part
 icipants will have an opportunity to gather in community as we honor thos
 e lost to HIV/AIDS\, recognize the resilience of people living with HIV\,
  and recommit ourselves to creating a more just and compassionate future.
 \nHIV & STI Testing (IU Health - Positive Link & Monroe County Health Dep
 artment) will be provided.\nAll Indiana University events\, groups\, acti
 vities\, educational\, cultural\, and historical observances welcome all 
 members of the Indiana University community.\n\nHosted by: LGBTQ+ Culture
  Center\n\nAdditional Information can be found at: https://beinvolved.ind
 iana.edu/event/12509443
DTEND:20261202T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20261114T061319Z
DTSTART:20261201T223000Z
GEO:39.164240;-86.521610
LOCATION:Biology Building Room 124
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:World AIDS Day - Keynote: Ace Robinson\, M.P.H.\, M.H.L.
UID:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12509443
URL:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12509443
X-HOSTS:LGBTQ+ Culture Center
END:VEVENT
